Your own use covers your private life and your own work, whether for your employer, your clients, or your own business. You may run the software on any computer, server, or cloud environment set up for you, including one provided by your employer. For example:

- You may be paid for work you do with the software, and deliver the results of that work.
- The software may contact other people on your behalf, such as by email or chat.
- Your employer, or someone you ask, may install and maintain the software for you, and may be paid for that work.
- Your family may use your setup for household matters.
- You may fork the official GitHub repository and publish changes in your fork in order to propose them to the licensor.

## Limitations

Unless the licensor gives you separate permission in writing (email is sufficient), you may not:

- sell the software, or provide it as part of a paid product or service;
